      "note": "Dusting"
    }
  ],
  "method": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "instruction": "Pan-fry veal in a little butter over medium-high heat until just cooked through, about 1–2 minutes per side. Remove and rest — veal toughens quickly if overdone."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "instruction": "In the same pan, fry bacon until beginning to crisp."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "instruction": "Add onion and capsicum and cook until softened, about 3–4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "instruction": "Add garlic and chilli if making the hot version. Cook for 30 seconds until fragrant."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "instruction": "Add diced tomato and cook down for 2–3 minutes until softened."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "instruction": "Pour in demi glace and thickened cream. Stir and reduce for 2–3 minutes until the sauce is rich and coats the back of a spoon."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "instruction": "Add green peppercorns and stir through. Return veal to the pan briefly to warm through."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "instruction": "Plate the veal and spoon the sauce generously over the top."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "technique",
      "title": "Hot or Mild",
      "content": "This dish is made to order — add chilli for the hot version, omit for mild. The green peppercorns provide a gentle warmth regardless, so the chilli determines the heat level."
    },
    {
      "type": "technique",
      "title": "Sauce Ratio",
      "content": "Equal parts cream to demi glace gives a balanced, rich sauce. No red wine is used in this preparation — the depth comes from the demi glace, bacon, and peppercorns."
    }
  ],
